.TH PLACE 1
.SH NAME
place \- put parts together into an assembly
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B place
.I assembly.txt
.SH DESCRIPTION
.I Place
reads an assembly file and writes the parts it names, renamed and
placed, as one fold file on the standard output.
Each line places one part:
.PP
.RS
.I name file.fold
[
.B rot
.I axis deg
] ... [
.B at
.I x y z
] [
.B colour
.I colour
]
.RE
.PP
Rotations are about the world axes through the origin, in order;
then the part is moved by
.RI ( x ,
.IR y ,
.IR z ).
Numbers are expressions as in
.IR sm (5).
A line
.B include
.I file
reads parameters, and
.B colours
.I file
reads a table of colours, one per line
.RI ( "name r g b roughness" ,
each from 0 to 1), to which a part's colour refers by name.
File names are relative to the assembly file; # starts a comment.
.SH SEE ALSO
interfere(1), fold(5), sm(5)
